{
  "name": "krita_paint_fill",
  "description": "Fill a shape on a paint layer with one flat antialiased colour, or reveal or hide it on a transparency mask, as one undo step: Krita's own fill, no brush dabs, painted with a fixed build-up stock preset. The shape is a rect, ellipse, polygon, closed curve or the current selection, and stays on the canvas. Checked against protection like a stroke and undone on a leak. Example: {\"type\": \"path\", \"points\": [[20, 20], [50, 26], [40, 46], [18, 40]]}.",
